1.Startup of the system:User must input a password
 1.1If password is wrong display Error message then ask again for the password
 1.2If password is right proceed to Enter your AEM{Student Id Number}
2.Menu Initialisation
 Uart Displays:
 a:Increase of reading frequency and printing by 1sec(minimum 2s)
 b:Decrease of reading frequency and printing by 1sec(maximum 10s)
 c:Change between Display Modes(Temperature/Humidity/Both)
 d:Printing of the latest values and the status of the system
 The Menu inputs can be inserted into the uart at any time!

3.Modes (switch between them with a simple button press)
 3.1Mode A The system reads and prints the Temperature and Humidity according to the User's settings
 3.2Mode B The system keeps reading and printing BUT if Temp reaches above 25% OR Humidity reaches above 60% Led starts blinking every 1sec
  3.2.2 In Mode B if the values return to normal the led keeps blinking for the first 5 readings/printings.Then it turns off

4.Dynamic change of frequency.Every 3rd time the button is pressed  there will be a new reading/printing frequency which will be the 2 last digits of the AEM added. F.e Aem=10852 then the new freq=7
5.UART Status Command:When status is inserted into the UART the system prints: "{Current Mode},{Last Temp/Humidity values},{Numbers of Mod swaps}"
6.Panic reset: If Temp>35% and Humidity>80% after 3 readings that violate the normal conditions the system has a software reset and prints a message!
